          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Grothendieck categories
            are those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                such that for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaves
                on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
                with values in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒜
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
                there is an existence theorem for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
                functor;
            %li
              %p
                such that all
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complexes"} complexes
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒜
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
                (with respect to a
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+translation"} translation
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphic
                to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+object"} homotopically injective
                complexes (so that
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor+on+a+derived+category"} derived functor
                can be computed on homotopically injective replacements).
          %p
            More abstractly, Grothendieck categories are precisely
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab-enriched"} Ab-enriched
            = succeed "es." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriel-Popescu+theorem"} Gabriel-Popescu theorem
            together with the theory of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+sheaves"} enriched sheaves
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            In terms of the AB
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            hierarchy discussed at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+and+abelian+categories"} additive and abelian categories
            we have
          %p
            A
            %strong Grothendieck category
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+and+abelian+categories"} AB5-category
            which has a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separator"} generator
          %p
            This means that a
            %strong Grothendieck category
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                that admits a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separator"} generator
            %li
              %p
                that admits small
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            %li
              %p
                such that small
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
                are
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} exact
                in the following sense:
              %ul
                %li
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direction"} directed set
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi B
                          %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \to A_i \to B_i \to C_i \to 0
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
                  for each
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi colim
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi colim
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi B
                          %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi colim
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \to colim_i A_i \to colim_i B_i \to colim_i C_i \to 0
                  is also an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
          %p
            Dually a
            %em co-Grothendieck category
            is an AB5
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ^*
            category with a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cogenerator"} cogenerator
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            A Grothendieck category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            satisfies the following properties.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                it admits small
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            %li
              %p
                if a functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C^{op} \to Set
                commutes with small
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                is
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
            %li
              %p
                if a functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C^{op} \to Set
                commutes with small
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                has a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} right adjoint
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriel-Popescu+theorem"} Gabriel-Popescu theorem
                exhibits any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+abelian+category"} Grothendieck abelian category
                as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+modules"} category of modules
                over a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %li
              %p
                Any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+abelian+category"} Grothendieck abelian category
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable"} locally presentable
              %p
                (
                %a{:href => "#Beke00"}> Beke (2000), Prop. 3.10
                , see also
                %a{:href => "#Krause"} Krause (2015), Corollary 5.2
                and references therein.)
            %li
              %p
                More generally, any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete"} cocomplete
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
                with a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators"} generators
                in which
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
                commute with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
                for some
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#PositselskiRosicky"} Positselski-Rosicky
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is equipped with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+translation"} translation
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mo :
                        %mi C
                        %mo →
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T : C \to C
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex"} complex
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Cplx
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in Cplx(C)
                there exists a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
                of
                = succeed "es" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex"} complex
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to I
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+object"} homotopically injective
            %li
              %p
                it satisfies Pierre Gabriel’s sup property: every small family of subobjects of a given object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                has a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supremum"} supremum
                which is a subobject of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %li
              %p
                it admits an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+object"} injective
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cogenerator"} cogenerator
                (see
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#KS"} Kashiwara-Schapira
          %p Much of the localization theory of rings generalizes to general Grothendieck categories.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
          #CateoriesOfModules.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
                is Grothendieck abelian)
              %br/
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+modules"} category of modules
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
              is a Grothendieck category. (See e.g
              %a{:href => "#Kiersz"} Kiersz 06, prop. 4
              for the proof that filtered colimits here are exact.) This statement remains true
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
              to any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone1977"}> Johnstone (1977), Thm. 8.11 (iii)
              \&amp;rbrack;.
          %p
          #CategoriesOfVectorSpaces.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
                is Grothendieck abelian)
              %br/
              Taking
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              in Exp.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CateoriesOfModules"}
              to be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              it follows that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+vector+spaces"} categories of vector spaces
              are Grothendieck abelian.
          %p
          #ChainComplexesInGrothAbCat.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ch
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒜
                          %mi Gr
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(\mathcal{A}_{Gr})
                is Grothendieck abelian)
              %br/
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              a Grothendieck category, the (unbounded)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(\mathcal{A})
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              is again a Grothendieck category (e.g.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Hovey99"} Hovey (1999), p. 3
            %p
              With Exp.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CateoriesOfModules"}
              it follows that the usual categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(R Mod)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              are all Grothendieck abelian.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+ind-objects"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ind
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒜
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ind(\mathcal{A})
                is Grothendieck abelian)
              %br/
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ind
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ind(\mathcal{A})
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ind-objects"} ind-objects
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a Grothendieck category.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+of+abelian+groups"} sheaf of abelian groups
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
          %h2#references References
          %p A dedicated survey is
          %ul
            %li
              Grigory Garkusha,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Grothendieck categories
              %a{:href => "https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Grigory_Garkusha/publication/2142579_Grothendieck_Categories/links/570e36d408aec783ddd1ba89.pdf"} pdf
          %p Grothendieck categories are mentioned at the end of section 8.3 in
          %ul
            %li#KS
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masaki+Kashiwara"}> Masaki Kashiwara
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Schapira"} Pierre Schapira
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+and+Sheaves"} Categories and Sheaves
          %p The relation to complexes is in section 14.1.
          %p
            The proof that filtered colimits in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Mod
            are exact is spelled out for instance in
          %ul
            %li#Kiersz
              Andy Kiersz,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Colimits and homological algebra
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/VIGRE/VIGRE2006/PAPERS/Kiersz.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Proof that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
            internal to any Grothendieck topos is Grothendieck abelian:
          %ul
            %li#Johnstone1977
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              \: Theorem 8.11 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topos+Theory"} Topos Theory
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Freyd"}> Peter Freyd
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Abelian categories
            %li
              %p
                Nicolae Popescu,
                %em An introduction to Abelian categories with applications to rings and modules
                %em , Academic Press 1973
          %p
            The fact that all Grothendieck categories are
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable"} locally presentable
          %ul
            %li#Beke00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tibor+Beke"}> Tibor Beke
                , Prop. 3.10 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Sheafifiable homotopy model categories
                %strong 129
                3 (2000) 447-475 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0102087"}> arXiv:math/0102087
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100004722"} doi:10.1017/S0305004100004722
            %li#Krause15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henning+Krause"}> Henning Krause
                , Corollary 5.2 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deriving Auslander’s formula
                %strong 20
                (2015) 669-688 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1409.7051"}> arXiv:1409.7051
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            A generalization to
            = succeed "-Grothendieck" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "-filtered" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
          %ul
            %li#PositselskiRosicky
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonid+Positselski"}> Leonid Positselski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Rosick%C3%BD"} Jiří Rosický
              = succeed "," do
                %em Covers, envelopes, and cotorsion theories in locally presentable abelian categories and contramodule categories
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.08119"} arXiv:1512.08119
          %p
            The duality of Grothendieck categories with categories of modules over
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linearly+compact+ring"} linearly compact ring
          %ul
            %li
              U. Oberst,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Duality theory for Grothendieck categories and linearly compact rings
              %strong 15
              (1970), p. 473 –542,
              %a{:href => "https://core.ac.uk/download/pdf/82581773.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structures+on+chain+complexes"} model structures on chain complexes
            in Grothendieck abelian categories is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              , F. Déglise,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Local and stable homologial algebra in Grothendieck abelian categories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.intlpress.com/HHA/v11/n1/a11/v11n1a11.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Formalization of Grothendieck categories as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+categories"} univalent categories
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+categories"} univalent categories
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+foundations+of+mathematics"}> univalent foundations of mathematics
            ):
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jarl+G.+Taxer%C3%A5s+Flaten"}> Jarl G. Taxerås Flaten
              , Section 3.1 in
              %em Univalent categories of modules
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2207.03261"}> arXiv:2207.03261
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p On Grothendieck abelian categories of chain complexes:
          %ul
            %li#Hovey99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Hovey"}> Mark Hovey
              , p. 3 of:
              %em Model category structures on chain complexes of sheaves
              (1999) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://faculty.math.illinois.edu/K-theory/0366"}> K-theory:0366
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://faculty.math.illinois.edu/K-theory/0366/sheaves.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Hovey-SheavesOfChainComplexesPreprint.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p which was published as
          %ul
            %li#Hovey01
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Hovey"}> Mark Hovey
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Model category structures on chain complexes of sheaves
              %strong 353
              6 (2001) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://www.ams.org/journals/tran/2001-353-06/S0002-9947-01-02721-0"}> ams:S0002-9947-01-02721-0
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/221954"} jstor:221954
          %p
            Two bicategories of
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategories+of+fractions"} bicategories of fractions
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Julia+Ramos+Gonz%C3%A1lez"}> Julia Ramos González
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Grothendieck categories as a bilocalization of linear sites
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10485-017-9511-1"} doi
        .revisedby
